# Setup: the Neon integration on each Vercel project

- setup-slug: neon-vercel-integration
- needs: database neon
- where: Vercel → the team → Storage, and each project → Settings → Environment Variables

## Why

The integration makes each preview's database: a Neon branch `preview/<git branch>`, made
before the build, and deleted with the git branch. No script of this build does it.
{%- if monorepo %}

The branch name comes from the git branch, not from the Vercel project.
So one pull request has one Neon branch, and each app of the pull request reads it. Connect
each app to the same Neon projects.
{%- endif %}

## Steps

Do these steps on each Vercel project of the build that reads the database:

1. Open Storage. Connect the Neon project `{% if uat %}uat-{% endif %}{{ slug }}` to the project, for the
   environment Preview only.
2. Turn on a database branch for each preview deployment.
3. Turn on the deletion of the branch when its git branch is deleted.
{%- if uat %}
4. Connect the Neon project `{{ slug }}` to the project, for the environment Production
   only. Or set `DATABASE_URL` and `DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED` of `{{ slug }}` on Production by
   hand.
5. Open Settings → Environment Variables. Make sure that Preview has no `DATABASE_URL` and no
   `DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED` for all branches.
6. Make sure that "Automatically expose System Environment Variables" is on.
{%- else %}
4. Connect the same project to the environment Production too.
5. Open Settings → Environment Variables. Make sure that Preview has no `DATABASE_URL` and no
   `DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED` for all branches.
6. Make sure that "Automatically expose System Environment Variables" is on.
{%- endif %}

## Done when

- [ ] A new pull request gets a Neon branch `preview/<git branch>` in `{% if uat %}uat-{% endif %}{{ slug }}`
      before its first build.
- [ ] Its preview build log shows `[vercel-build] VERCEL_TARGET_ENV=preview: migrate, verify,
      then build`.
{%- if monorepo %}
- [ ] A pull request that changes two apps gets one Neon branch, and the build log of each app
      shows the endpoint of that branch, not the endpoint of the default branch.
{%- endif %}
- [ ] Preview has no `DATABASE_URL` for all branches.
- [ ] Production reads `{{ slug }}`.
